 \\\\ y-x+6z \\\\ 8z-x+3y\\end{aligned}],$ find its rank." 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186125156 1074 "First, the standard matrix of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(T))=\\text{rank}(T).$ \n\nSo, we need to find the rank of the matrix $T.$ We reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 8\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{5}{3}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $T$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=3.\n$$" 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129093 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326716 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129100 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326727 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129100 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326728 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129101 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326768 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129102 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326780 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129102 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326788 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129102 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326812 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129108 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326906 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129119 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326929 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129122 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326686 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129125 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326701 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186129125 1038 #edb/ref 17592186326702 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186