r the set $H:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {h}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {h}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot (-4)+1\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 3=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥H.$\n\n- For the set $V:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {v}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-3)=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {v}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-4)+(-1)\\cdot (-2)=-3\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥̸V.$ Notice that we stopped after finding the first non-orthogonal vector in the set.\n\n- For the set $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot {w}_{1} & =(-1)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 5+(-1)\\cdot 8=0 & ✓ \\\\ u\\cdot {w}_{2} & =(-1)\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot 2=0 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $u⊥W.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\"" 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134236 1068 #edb/ref 17592186131425 13194139533422 17592186045585 false] [17592186134236 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326348 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134236 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134236 1071 "Consider the vector subspace $H = Span{\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}$. Which of the following vectors belong to $H^{⊥}$?\n$v_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}, v_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}, v_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533422 17592186045585 false] [17592186134236 1071 "Consider the vector subspace $H=\\text{Span}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}.$ Which of the following vectors belong to ${H}^{⊥}?$\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134236 1074 "Let's denote the vectors that span the subspace $H$