in{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ -3\\cdot 1+a\\cdot 1+b\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot (-4) & =0 \\\\ -3+a-3b+16 & =0 \\\\ a-3b & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4a+b=13 \\\\ a-3b=-13\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13a=26\\,⟹\\,a=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(2)+b & =13 \\\\ 8+b & =13 \\\\ b & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b=2+5=7.\n$$" 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134259 1068 #edb/ref 17592186131563 13194139533422 17592186045585 false] [17592186134259 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326537 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134259 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134259 1071 "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of $R^{3}$ onto the subspace spanned by $a = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139533422 17592186045585 false] [17592186134259 1071 "Find a matrix that defines the orthogonal projection of ${R}^{3}$ onto the subspace spanned by $a=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134259 1074 "Recall that the matrix ${P}_{S}=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}$ maps any vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ onto its orthogonal projection in the subspace $S$ spanned by the columns of the matrix $A.$ \n\nIn our case, $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(14)^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned