ligned}6 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\overset{^}{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\overset{^}{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\overset{^}{x}-b & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\overset{^}{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{30}.\n$$" 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134374 1068 #edb/ref 17592186132253 13194139533422 17592186045585 false] [17592186134374 1068 #edb/ref 17592186326409 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134374 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134374 1071 "Given that $F = 2xy^{2}i + 4x^{2}yj$, what is $divF$?" 13194139533422 17592186045585 false] [17592186134374 1071 "Given that $F=2x{y}^{2}\\,i+4{x}^{2}y\\,j,$ what is $\\text{div}\\,F?$" 13194139533422 17592186045585 true] [17592186134374 1074 "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the divergence of $F$ is the scalar field given by\n\n$$\n\\text{div}\\,F=∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\cdot F & =\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4{x}^{2}y) \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}+4{x}^{2} \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}.\\end